Telling what an allocation would take needs RIGHT_W on the pool, as allocating does;
a pool tells it to any holder.

Caught-by: fuzz fuzz-pmp8 fuzz-rp2350 fuzz-smp2 fuzz-work qemu-replay
Report: a describing call failed on a filled slot

diff --git a/kernel/syscall.c b/kernel/syscall.c
--- a/kernel/syscall.c
+++ b/kernel/syscall.c
@@ -1021,7 +1021,7 @@ static int dispatch(struct thread *t, uint32_t op, uint32_t slot, uint32_t *arg)
         err = (cap.rights & RIGHT_W) ? op_captable(t, slot, &cap, op, arg) : KERR_NO_RIGHTS;
         break;
     case CAP_POOL:
-        err = (op == OP_POOL_INFO || (cap.rights & RIGHT_W)) ? op_pool(t, slot, &cap, op, arg) : KERR_NO_RIGHTS;
+        err = (cap.rights & RIGHT_W) ? op_pool(t, slot, &cap, op, arg) : KERR_NO_RIGHTS;
         break;
     case CAP_PROCESS:
         err = (cap.rights & RIGHT_W) ? op_process(t, &cap, op, arg) : KERR_NO_RIGHTS;
